# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SafeZone environment variables
# Copy this file to .env.local for local dev, or set these in
# Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# OPTIONAL — Google Maps Embed API key.
#
# The app works WITHOUT this: it falls back to the free keyless Google
# Maps embed, which renders a real, accurate map out of the box.
#
# Provide a key to use the official Maps Embed API (recommended at scale,
# more reliable, custom styling later):
#   1. https://console.cloud.google.com  → create / pick a project
#   2. APIs & Services → Library → enable "Maps Embed API"
#   3. APIs & Services → Credentials → Create credentials → API key
#   4. Restrict the key to your domain (HTTP referrers) for safety
#   5. Add it in Vercel as NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY and redeploy
#
# NOTE: NEXT_PUBLIC_ vars are exposed to the browser by design (the map
# loads client-side). Always restrict the key by HTTP referrer.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
